<title>USA: FP&amp;L St. Lucie 1 nuke at 77 pct power - NRC.</title>
<headline>FP&amp;L St. Lucie 1 nuke at 77 pct power - NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida Power &amp; Light Co's 839 megawatt (MW) St Lucie 1 nuclear unit in Hutchinson Island, Fla., is operating at 77 percent power Friday, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said in its morning report.</p>
<p>The NRC said power at the unit was reduced to repair &quot;the main condenser water box tube.&quot;</p>
<p>The company was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>St Lucie 2, also with a generating capacity of 839 MW, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
</text>
